      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg/day is double the maximum labeled dose of 2,550 mg/day. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient. A hospital order-entry system also shouldn't be the only check on a dose like this.\n- **I still don't have a prescriber's authorization.** You've told me you aren't a clinician, so your confirmation can't stand in for the treating prescriber's.\n\n**What will work:**\n- The treating prescriber can enter the order themselves or tell me the intended dose. If they really do want a dose above the labeled maximum, they should document the clinical reason and have pharmacy review it.\n- If the dose was a typo, I can enter a corrected dose right away. Examples are 850 mg three times daily with meals, or 1000 mg twice daily with meals.\n\nTell me the corrected dose, or have the prescriber contact me, and I'll enter it."
      }
